before(76,'6.1.1 Independent implementation audit and coordination liability','Heading 3')
before(76,'The v3 audit (audit/reproduce_audit.py; results/independent_audit.json) exhaustively tests the 64 × 64 six-bit operand pairs in each architecture, in batches of 64, for 16,384 correct products in total. Across six network sizes and 30 seeds, each of three reused architectures was also compared against dedicated circuits on every one of the 4,096 binary input states: 540 comparisons with zero output-bit mismatches. This verifies functional equivalence for the modeled workloads, not complete CPU fidelity or biological validity.')
before(76,'The code-space estimates (92, 388, 385 and 378 tasks) are limited by the actual fixed operand/result layout, which reserves 128 entries per table. With the deterministic capacity workload in the audit, the longest consecutive successful runs were 92 tasks inlined and 128 in each reused architecture. At task 129 the reused designs exhibit output errors; the estimate of 388 tasks therefore cannot be presented as demonstrated workload capacity.')
before(76,'Table 3a. Expanded fault audit at N = 64. Mean disrupted tasks per NOP injection, including timeouts, and number of tested routine and other tracked instruction sites. Faults in untracked page transitions, final halt, data memory and physical hardware remain excluded.')
