for a,label in [('inlined','Inlined'),('shared','Shared'),('dual_modular','Dual modular'),('buffered_tmr','Redundant fallback')]:
    v=audit[a];r=v['faults']['routine'];o=v['faults']['other_tracked'];rows.append([label,v['consecutive_capacity'],f"{r['mean_blast']:.2f} ({r['fault_sites']})",f"{o['mean_blast']:.2f} ({o['fault_sites']})",f"{r['timeouts']} / {o['timeouts']}"])
table_before(76,['Architecture','Working tasks','Routine mean (n)','Other mean (n)','Timeouts R/O'],rows)
before(76,'The wider audit reveals a second-order architectural trade-off: protective coordination can itself be vulnerable. Other tracked instructions include input/output handling and the redundant comparison wrapper, so their impact cannot be attributed exclusively to the wrapper. A future analysis should stratify fault sites by role, distinguish missing outputs from incorrect outputs, include stuck-on and correlated failures, and report uncertainty under multiple operand sets and workloads. The present metric uses zero-initialized outputs and a minimum of one affected task on timeout; noncompletion and incorrect numerical output must be separately recorded in subsequent work.')
before(76,'Pooling the enumerated routine and other tracked sites with equal weight per site changes the ranking (Figure 9): mean disruption is 8.47 tasks for inlining, 16.28 for sharing, 16.10 for dual modularity and 13.03 for redundant fallback. These are descriptive averages under a deliberately limited uniform site-injection model, not field failure probabilities. The redundant design remains more economical in code than inlining but is not more reliable on this pooled metric. This negative result is central to the argument: a protection architecture must be evaluated together with its coordination overhead.')
fig_before(76,'fig9_fault_scope.png','Figure 9. Sensitivity of PDP-8 fault results to the scope of injection. A: separate mean impacts for enumerated routine words and other tracked executable words. B: pooled mean, weighting each tested site equally. Timeouts included; data-memory faults and untracked instructions excluded. Derived from results/independent_audit.json.')
replace(82,'R(e) — Local buffering: primary measure should be independently estimated co-active alternate-enhancer capacity, ideally functional attenuation from matched single and combined perturbations. Raw (unnormalized) activity × contact for alternate elements can serve as a secondary proxy [12,17]. Normalized ABC scores sum to a constrained denominator; the sum of the other scores can be approximately 1 − ABC(e), so it is not an independent demonstration of redundancy. Report that proxy as a sensitivity analysis only and distinguish compensatory from additive effects.')
replace(96,'Nested model ladder: evaluate global absolute predictions on held-out chromosomes and within-target-gene contrasts separately. Train-fold-only preprocessing, prespecified thresholds and spatially aware uncertainty estimation are required:')
replace(107,'P4 (out-of-sample predictive gain): Global M2 improves absolute outcome prediction over global M1 on held-out chromosomes; within-gene M2b improves within-gene contrast prediction over M1b. The second task does not predict an unseen gene intercept. Report performance and uncertainty separately across sensitivity checks.')
replace(108,'A sufficiently precise null or opposite association in a well-powered, appropriately measured test would count against H2; failure due to inadequate data coverage, poor proxy validity or lack of within-gene variation would remain inconclusive. The computational findings about H1 do not imply H2.')
before(103,'Validation clarification. The v3 implementation (genomics/validation_v3.py) fits scaling on training chromosomes only. Global held-out predictions are absolute; gene-centered predictions on held-out groups are evaluated only against observed within-gene contrasts. A fixed effect for an unseen gene cannot be estimated without additional information. For inference, report gene-cluster and genomic-block sensitivity analyses, refitting the estimator within each resample rather than reusing a globally transformed design. Quantify how much B and R vary within each gene across contexts; if variation is insufficient, the within-gene test is unidentified. K562 is a cancer-derived line and must not be treated as representative of mammalian development; validate across matched developmental contexts when possible. Perturb-seq [30] supplies a candidate perturbational data source; it does not itself establish H2.')
before(103,'Synthetic software check. The v3 validation script reproduces the intended distinction in two artificial fixtures (1,189 enhancers each): within-gene contrast MSE changes from 0.4435 to 0.4468 when no coordination effect is simulated, and from 0.5909 to 0.4561 when a coordination effect is simulated. Global prediction gains can occur under confounding. These are software checks, not evidence about real enhancers; the genomic data acquisition and harmonization pipeline remains proposed.')
replace(116,'Population-genetic drift limits: weakly selected costs can be overwhelmed by drift, particularly in small effective populations [23,24]. The relative evolutionary importance of extra nucleotides, expression costs and developmental perturbation remains an empirical question; architecture may be economical along some axes but not others.')
replace(120,'The DEC PDP-8 shows that a small repertoire of operations can support rich functionality through reuse. The cost of that economy is shared dependence. In the two computational models, bounded reuse and targeted redundancy reduce selected failure consequences, but verification, control flow and other supporting machinery contribute vulnerabilities of their own. Thus the proposed cross-domain principle is not that all systems are optimized, but that economy, coordination, resilience and adaptability must be evaluated together.')
replace(121,'The genomic implication is a testable question, not an established biological law: does higher-order regulatory reach, moderated by independently measured buffering, explain additional evolutionary constraint beyond enhancer pleiotropy and target-gene identity? The computational findings motivate this empirical investigation without substituting for it. If the prediction fails under an adequate test, the biological extension must be revised or rejected. A useful architecture is one in which the organization of parts, not just their number, accounts for the capacity and vulnerability of the whole.')
replace(125,'Code and data availability: the accompanying repository package includes original v2 sources and result JSON, all figures, the v3 audit source and raw fault counts, the v3 synthetic validation script and results, prior manuscript versions and reproduction instructions. Repository: https://github.com/RandoSY/architectural-economy (full package pending upload); archival DOI pending. No empirical genomic dataset or result is claimed.')
replace(127,'Author affiliation: Independent Researcher, Indiana, USA. ORCID: https://orcid.org/0009-0003-1657-0243. Correspondence details to be confirmed before journal submission.')
replace(128,'Generative AI disclosure: ChatGPT assisted literature discovery, synthesis, illustrations, drafting, independent computational checks and editing; Google Gemini/Antigravity assisted critical editing, model refinement and computational implementation. AI-assisted figures are labeled conceptual or derived from code outputs, as appropriate. The author must review the manuscript, references, code, figures and disclosures and confirm responsibility before submission. No independent human peer review has occurred.')
